    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** (75.54) anchoring the lineup, benefiting from a high-ceiling matchup against Mason Barnett. The combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and prime positioning in the #3 hole elevates **Caminero** well above his base projection. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.63) and **Yordan Alvarez** (67.60) serve as our primary engines; **Crow-Armstrong** remains a vital asset for his elite speed profile in our quest for scarce stolen bases, while **Alvarez** benefits from favorable wind conditions that bolster his power floor. **Trea Turner** (66.35) also demands attention, as his matchup against Andre Pallante offers a rare opportunity to exploit a slow delivery for stolen base upside, further reinforcing our aggressive tactical approach on the basepaths.\n\nPlatoon edges are instrumental in our starting rotation today, most notably for **Christian Yelich** (66.99) and **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16), both of whom see significant score inflation due to favorable right-handed matchups. **Nootbaar** in particular receives a massive +19% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s skill set, making him an ideal start against Tomoyuki Sugano. Our most difficult decision on the bench was **Nelson Velazquez** (50.83), who fell just shy of the threshold. While **Velazquez** benefits from positive wind variables, the optimizer prioritized the higher floor and positional stability offered by **Carson Benge** (53.28), despite the latter\u2019s platoon disadvantage. As we finalize these spots, managers should note that all projected lineup positions remain pending; any late-breaking shifts in batting order\u2014particularly for **Dillon Dingler** or **Gary Sanchez**\u2014could necessitate a final re-evaluation of our efficiency rankings before first pitch.",
